    <item>
      <title>Hello World.ko</title>
      <link>https://jlmunix.github.io/my-notes/posts/linux/modules/hello_world/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 29 Sep 2025 15:30:00 -0400</pubDate>
      <guid>https://jlmunix.github.io/my-notes/posts/linux/modules/hello_world/</guid>
      <description>&lt;!-- markdownlint-disable MD033 --&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-hello-world-module-to-start&#34;&gt;Simple hello world module to start&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This hello world kernel module has been developed as a starting point.
It is also considered that a &lt;strong&gt;buildroot(BR)&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;kernel(external to BR)&lt;/strong&gt; has been previously
built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&#34;img-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;images/Linux/structure.png&#34;
         alt=&#34;Description&#34;/&gt; &lt;figcaption&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;File structure of buildroot and linux&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&#34;prerequisites&#34;&gt;Prerequisites&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before we start, ensure you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buildroot environment&lt;/strong&gt; properly configured and built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QEMU virtualization&lt;/strong&gt; setup for your target architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External Linux kernel&lt;/strong&gt; built with module support enabled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-compilation toolchain&lt;/strong&gt; (provided by Buildroot)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;external-kernel-configuration&#34;&gt;External Kernel Configuration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since you&amp;rsquo;re using an external kernel, module support must be enabled in your &lt;strong&gt;kernel configuration&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
